      "problem": "Express $\\frac{36}{25}$ as a base raised to a negative exponent.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $\\frac{36}{25}$ as a base raised to a power:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{36}{25} & =\\frac{6\\times 6}{5\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\times \\frac{6}{5} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{6}{5})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the reciprocal of the base $(\\frac{6}{5}),$ and then raise that reciprocal to the same power but with the *opposite* sign $(-2),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{2}={(\\frac{5}{6})}^{-2}\n$$",
